# CMake and tests

## gameLib sources

Every new implementation `.cpp` under `src/` must be added to the `gameLib` source list in `src/CMakeLists.txt`. Omitting it means the file never compiles.

Executable is `game` (`src/main.cpp`); link only against `gameLib` + SFML as already set up.

## Tests (Debug only)

```sh
cmake --preset debug
cmake --build --preset debug --target build_ut
ctest --preset debug
```

- Unit tests: `tests/unit_tests/` (`smoke_test`, `fixed_timestep_test`, `iscreen_dummy_test`, `screen_stack_test`, `screen_transition_test`, `input_mapper_test`, `pause_blocks_ticks_test`, `world_test`, `rect_collision_test`, `arkanoid_session_test`); GoogleTest 1.18 via FetchContent
- Register with `add_unit_test(...)` in `tests/unit_tests/CMakeLists.txt`
- Prefer tests that do not open a window unless a display is required
- Fixture names like `*Should` when adding behavioral suites

When changing `gameLib`, update or add unit tests in `tests/unit_tests/`.
